-- Outreach v6 (owner, 2026-10-16): open with the problem, add urgency and a
-- real ask. Every first email names the two costs (after-hours calls going to
-- voicemail, and not being found on Google: the verified {issue_line}), and
-- every email ends on {booking_line}: a 15-minute booking link when
-- settings.outreach.booking_url is set, else "reply with a time". No fake
-- deadlines or scarcity. Copy only; caps and switches are unchanged.
-- Re-runnable: it overwrites the same keys each time. The mailing address is
-- added by the code from the private business_mailing_address row.

update settings set value = jsonb_set(jsonb_set(jsonb_set(jsonb_set(jsonb_set(value,
    '{touch_sets}', (value->'touch_sets') || $j${"website": [{"step": 1, "delay_days": 0, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi,\n\nTwo things are probably costing {business_name} customers every week:\n\n1. Calls after you close. Someone needs you at 7 p.m., gets voicemail, and calls the next name on Google instead. Plenty of them never call back.\n2. Being found. Your website {issue_line}. Small gaps like that are where people searching on Google give up and pick a competitor.\n\nI already made a free sample of a better site for you: {preview_url}\n\nWade Capital fixes both, at one fixed price:\n- an AI phone agent that answers after hours, says it's an AI, takes the caller's details and books the appointment\n- a website built to be found on Google and turn searches into calls\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}], "both": [{"step": 1, "delay_days": 0, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi,\n\nTwo things are probably costing {business_name} customers every week:\n\n1. Calls after you close. Someone needs you at 7 p.m., gets voicemail, and calls the next name on Google instead. Plenty of them never call back.\n2. Being found. Your website {issue_line}. Small gaps like that are where people searching on Google give up and pick a competitor.\n\nI already made a free sample of a better site for you: {preview_url}\n\nWade Capital fixes both, at one fixed price:\n- an AI phone agent that answers after hours, says it's an AI, takes the caller's details and books the appointment\n- a website built to be found on Google and turn searches into calls, with social media that posts on its own\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}], "no_website": [{"step": 1, "delay_days": 0, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi,\n\nTwo things are probably costing {business_name} customers every week:\n\n1. Calls after you close. Someone needs you at 7 p.m., gets voicemail, and calls the next name on Google instead. Plenty of them never call back.\n2. Being found. I searched for {business_name} and couldn't find a website, so anyone comparing options on Google only sees your competitors' sites.\n\nSo I made a free mockup of one for you, built from your Google listing: {preview_url}\n\nWade Capital fixes both, at one fixed price:\n- an AI phone agent that answers after hours, says it's an AI, takes the caller's details and books the appointment\n- a website built to be found on Google and turn searches into calls\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}], "social": [{"step": 1, "delay_days": 0, "subject": "missed calls at {business_name}", "body": "Hi,\n\nTwo things are probably costing {business_name} customers every week:\n\n1. Calls after you close. Someone needs you at 7 p.m., gets voicemail, and calls the next name on Google instead. Plenty of them never call back.\n2. Being seen. Your website {issue_line}, and a lot of customers check Instagram or Facebook before they visit. A page that posts every week is often what tips them your way.\n\nWade Capital fixes both, at one fixed price:\n- an AI phone agent that answers after hours, says it's an AI, takes the caller's details and books the appointment\n- social media that posts on its own (I can make a free sample week of posts for {business_name} first)\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}]}$j$::jsonb),
    '{followups}', $j$[{"step": 2, "delay_days": 4, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, quick follow-up. Tonight, after {business_name} closes, the phone will still ring, and unless someone is there to pick up, those calls go to voicemail.{mockup_line}\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}, {"step": 3, "delay_days": 7, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, one more idea. If a full project feels like a lot right now, we can start with just the after-hours phone agent: it answers every call {business_name} would otherwise miss, books the appointment, and emails you a summary by morning. One fixed price.\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}, {"step": 4, "delay_days": 10, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, I'll close your file after this one. If missed calls or getting found on Google becomes a priority for {business_name}, just reply \"yes\" and I'll send you a few times.\n\n{sender_name}"}]$j$::jsonb),
    '{automation_pivot,touches}', $j$[{"step": 3, "delay_days": 7, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, one more idea. If a full project feels like a lot right now, we can start with just the after-hours phone agent: it answers every call {business_name} would otherwise miss, books the appointment, and emails you a summary by morning. One fixed price.\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}, {"step": 4, "delay_days": 10, "subject": "missed calls and Google at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, I'll close your file after this one. If missed calls or getting found on Google becomes a priority for {business_name}, just reply \"yes\" and I'll send you a few times.\n\n{sender_name}"}]$j$::jsonb),
    '{touch_sets,governance_audit}', $j$[{"step": 1, "delay_days": 0, "subject": "after-hours calls and court deadlines at {business_name}", "body": "Hi,\n\nTwo things quietly cost small firms clients and sleep:\n\n1. The new-client call at 7 p.m. that goes to voicemail. That caller usually tries the next firm on Google, and the case goes with them.\n2. Court deadlines that live in one person's inbox, one sick day away from a missed filing.\n\nI'm Deven, and I run Wade Capital with a few Penn State Business, IT, and Law students. For law firms we set up:\n- an after-hours intake agent that answers every call, says it's an AI, takes the caller's details and matter type, flags anything urgent, and emails you a summary (it never gives legal advice)\n- deadline and docket tracking: every court date and filing deadline in one calendar, with reminders to the attorney and a backup\n- a written AI use policy, so staff use these tools within Rules 1.1, 1.6 and 5.3\n\n{context}Each is a fixed price.\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}]$j$::jsonb),
    '{followup_sets,governance_audit}', $j$[{"step": 2, "delay_days": 4, "subject": "after-hours calls at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, bumping this in case it got buried.\n\nHere's the intake agent in practice: someone calls {business_name} at 9 p.m., hears they've reached the firm's AI assistant, gives their name, number and what happened, and you have a summary in your inbox before morning, with anything urgent at the top. No new client lost to voicemail, and no legal advice given.\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}, {"step": 3, "delay_days": 7, "subject": "court deadlines at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, one more idea: deadline and docket tracking.\n\nEvery court date, filing deadline and limitations date your team enters goes into one shared calendar, with reminders at 30, 7 and 1 days to the responsible attorney and a backup. Your team still confirms every date; the system makes sure nobody forgets one.\n\n{booking_line}\n\n{sender_name}"}, {"step": 4, "delay_days": 10, "subject": "court deadlines at {business_name}", "body": "Hi, I'll close your file after this one. If after-hours intake, deadline tracking, or an AI use policy becomes a priority for {business_name}, just reply \"yes\" and I'll send you a few times.\n\n{sender_name}"}]$j$::jsonb, true)
where key = 'outreach';
